WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.800 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hey, everybody.

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
We are joined now by
one of my favorite comedians

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:06.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
a great guy,
and he has a YouTube show

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.374 line:92%
that he started this last month,

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:09.943
called "Dinner with the J-
Dinner with the Gaffigans.

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:12.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's "Gaffigan," right?
not "Jaffigan"?

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.748 line:92%
-Sometimes it's Jaffigan.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:15.815 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:18.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We're here with Jim Gaffigan.
Hi, Jim.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:21.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi.
It's nice to talk to you.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:24.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
I -- I'm not sure
exactly where you are,

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:26.760 line:92%
but I am in downtown Manhattan

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:34.801
My wife is high-risk, so we ar
under double-secret quarantine

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.870 line:92%
I am with my five children

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've been here for a month,
and they're still alive.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.810 line:92%
So I should get an award.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:44.677 line:92%
-You should get an award.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.379
I mean,
don't take this the wrong way --

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've always thought
that you were a little crazy

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.150 line:92%
that you have five children,

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.786 size:75% position:38%
you travel with them
everywhere you go.

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:55.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're incredible
parents to them.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:58.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you must be regretting i
a little bit right now.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.293 line:92%
-I'm absolutely regretting it.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:04.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think if there's
one takeaway from this segment

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:08.768
it should be to encourage people
not to have children.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:13.373 size:78% position:39%
And if you have them,
give them away now.

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:18.211
No, I -- It's this thing
called distance learning,

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is -- obviously,
the schools have shut down

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:23.650 size:78% position:39%
and distance learning
was created by people

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.385 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that truly hate parents.

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:28.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I have five kids,
so you'd think,

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.256 size:88% position:44% line:92%
five kids, five screens,

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:34.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
five places
in a New York City apartment

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:35.962 size:84% position:42% line:92%
But it's not even that.

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:40.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's five different schedule
for five different kids

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
on five different screens
in a New York City apartment

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:47.740
And the school, they just send
these kind of assignments, like,

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, have your 7-year-old
do all this stuff."

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:52.946 line:92%
I'm like, "I'm not doing this.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:55.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm raising them
to be farmhands.

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:58.751
-You have -- I think, if I hav
it right, three boys, two girls?

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are they handling it
differently?

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.523 line:92%
-The girls are civilized.

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:06.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
The boys, who only want
to play on iPads,

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:08.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
once it comes
to their distance learning

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:13.199
which is essentially
teleconferencing with a teacher,

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:16.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
that suddenly, they don't know
how to turn on a computer.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:17.370 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You know what I mean?

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or the iPad
is confusing to them.

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I understand,
it's difficult.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:24.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
school without friends,

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:26.980 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that's appealing, right?

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:27.981 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right, sure.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:29.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are they getting
their work done?

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:34.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you a taskmaster with them
-You know, I --

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:36.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
It's too --

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:36.956 line:92%
There's too many of them,

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:39.192 size:75% position:38%
and there's too many
different projects.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I think, yesterday
I spent two hours

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:48.902
trying to print from my son'
school iPad to our printer

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:51.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I know that I printed out
the assignment.

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:54.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
what happened to it, though.

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
He'll be fine.
-So at the end of the day,

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
you don't sort of gather the
all around and say,

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:00.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Let's show me
what you've done?"

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:03.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not really. No.
You know, eventually,

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:09.255
it gets to 6:00 p.m., we d
"Dinner with the Gaffigans,"

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:12.258 line:92%
and then, I pretend to like them

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
for like 40 minutes
during the show.

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:17.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
By the way, we've done,
I think, 26 --

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:21.501 size:84% position:42%
we've done a whole --
we've done 28 episodes.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:24.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's crazy.
-That's a whole season.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:25.605 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You know what I mean?

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:27.707 size:78% position:39%
-That's like a season
back in like 1950.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right? I don't know
if we've been picked up.

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:32.779
I don't think -- I don't want us
to get picked up.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:37.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
But there is --
you know, it's like --

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we don't really
have contracts,

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:43.423
so my kids could come back
and really have high demands

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:45.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I think
you could threaten --

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:49.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of sitcoms
replace child actors.

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:49.629 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's true.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:52.232
-This is basically you jus
filming family and dinner.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, where did you
get this idea?

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.802 line:92%
-I was on tour in Latin America.

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:59.606
I was in Bogotá, and I was about
to head to the theater,

00:03:59.606 --> 00:04:03.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my manager called me
and informed me that Argentina

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:07.947
had closed its borders, so I
would not be going to Argentina.

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:10.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
things were moving fast.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:14.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I decided to fly back hom
the next day.

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:17.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
And while I was at the airport
there was a --

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:20.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I was existing
with the knowledge

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:23.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I might not get back,
or I might be separated

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:26.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
from my family
for an extended time.

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:29.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, the
"Dinner with the Gaffigans

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:33.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
was something that serves
as just --

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:34.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause I know that
there are some people

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:38.444
separated from their families,
or they're just by themselves.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have friends
that are by themselves.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.382 line:92%
So it was just something light

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:46.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
and also, it would be somethin
to serve as a break

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:51.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the constant, you know,
consumption of news.

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:54.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I don't know
how many times --

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like, at this point
there's got to be three or fou

00:04:57.163 --> 00:05:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sanjay Guptas,
because that poor guy,

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:03.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's working so hard.
-Yeah.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And all those CNN anchors
they're like,

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:07.573 line:92%
"My friend, Sanjay Gupta..."

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:10.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
He doesn't
like any of those people now

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:10.710 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.578
-They're like,
"Sanjay, can you be on my show?"

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:16.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "I haven't slep
in three weeks."

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:18.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, but we wanted
"Dinner with the Gaffigans,"

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.887 line:92%
which is streamed on YouTube

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:23.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it has
an interactive element,

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:27.193 line:92%
so people can ask families

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:29.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we do charades
and stuff like that.

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:33.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's totally
a distraction from, you know

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:34.701 size:88% position:44% line:92%
what we're dealing with.

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to --
We're gonna put up a photo

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:40.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
of sort of a typical
"Dinner with the Gaffigans,"

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:43.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, I want to put up
a second photo where

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:45.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
it looks as though
your youngest son

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:48.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
is wearing a Spider-Man mask
-Yes.

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:51.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, was that
for the whole dinner?

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:53.286 line:92%
-Well, there's different themes.

00:05:53.286 --> 00:05:56.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not for the whole dinner.
But there's different themes

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:57.457 line:92%
One -- and by the way, it's --

00:05:57.457 --> 00:06:00.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
the enthusiasm from my childre
has disappeared.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Do you guys
want to dress up

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:03.763 line:92%
since we're having bratwurst

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:05.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you want
to do German things?"

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:06.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're like,
"No, get outta here."

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:10.503
But there was a dress-up,
like, a superhero dinner,

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:13.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Patrick was the only one
that dressed up.

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.440 line:92%
But what we've done recently

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:17.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
probably for the past
week or two,

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:19.212 line:92%
